//! Routines that make one choice and act on it.
//!
//! 4469 of them: a single question at the top, a run of calls on one side, some of
//! them a run on the other, and no loop anywhere. What is recorded is the
//! question, both runs, and whether anything is worked out besides the calls —
//! because where something is, the calls are not the whole story and the entry
//! says so.
//!
//! The questions asked here lean the opposite way from the ones in
//! [`crate::guarded_routines`]. There, most guards ask whether something **is**
//! there and do the work if it is. Here, most ask whether something is **not**
//! there and act on that — an early answer for the empty case, with the real
//! work left to fall through. The two families are the same test written the two
//! ways round, and which way round it is written says which case the author
//! thought of as the exception.

// The addresses are written without separators so the port-mapping importer can
// match them against the recovered functions.
#![allow(clippy::unreadable_literal)]

pub use crate::guarded_routines::Asks;

/// One routine that makes a single choice.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy)]
pub struct Choice {
    /// Where it sits.
    pub routine: u32,
    /// What the question is.
    pub asks: Asks,
    /// What it calls when the answer is yes.
    pub when_yes: &'static [u32],
    /// What it calls when the answer is no, where it calls anything.
    pub when_no: &'static [u32],
    /// Whether it also works something out that the calls do not show.
    pub also_computes: bool,
    /// Whether anything is called after the choice has been made.
    pub calls_after: bool,
    /// Whether anything is called before the question is asked.
    pub calls_before: bool,
}

